<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhŏdănus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The Rhone</i>, <i>a river in
			Gaul</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 5, 4 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4,
				5, § 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
				446 sq.</span></i>; Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 10,
				7, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 1, 1</span></i>; Planc. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 9, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 11, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				258</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21, 26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhodani potor,</span>”
				<i>a dweller by the Rhone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 20, 20</span></i>
			 et saep.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> RHODANICI NAVTAE, <i>sailors</i> or <i>boatmen on the Rhone</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 809</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4110</span></i>; in
				sing., <i><span class="en">id. ib.
			4223</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhŏdănītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Rhone</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbes,</span>”
				<i>situated upon the Rhone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. Carm. 9, 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhŏdănū-sĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>the Rhone
			City</i>, Lugdunum, now <i>Lyons</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 5 <i>init.</i></span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>the dwellers by the
				Rhone</i>, <i>the Gauls</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rheno Rhodanoque subactis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					5, 268</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
